      "leadImage": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/c/c2/GK%26C_St_Peter%27s_chapel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled",
      "source": "Wikipedia"
    },
    "town": {
      "title": "Cardross",
      "description": "Village in Argyll and Bute, Scotland",
      "extract": "Cardross is a large village with a population of 2,032 (2022) in Scotland, on the north side of the Firth of Clyde, situated halfway between Dumbarton and Helensburgh. Cardross is in the historic geographical county of Dunbartonshire but the modern political local authority of Argyll and Bute.",
      "url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cardross",
